/-!
# Two-point tori and root generation in the actual unitary carriers

For every SU₃ or PSU₃ Sylow subgroup and outside involution, the two-point
torus and its fixed subgroup are cyclic with their exact source orders.
The literal commutator torus is cyclic of order q-1 and is inverted
elementwise; every inside/outside involution pair has odd centralizer.

The subgroup generated by Ω₁(P) and the outside involution is concretely
isomorphic to PSL₂(q), and is generated by any nonidentity involution of P,
the outside involution, and the commutator torus. Genuine inner pair
normalization transports the fixed-field matrix calculation to every pair,
retaining the original SU₃ carrier as well as its projective quotient.

Source: GLS4, Chapter 4, Lemma 3.2(c)-(e),(h),(i), and Chapter 2, Section 16.
-/
